    "done_when": "Done when. Tests with a temporary repository and crew home show the following: A review whose worker never launched stays queued. An in-progress review is not promotable. A delivered design review's findings are listed with ids before any promotion. A code-mode review promotes. A record stored under its plain name is accepted by promotion as by the check. A census, written to the section's evidence fragment, takes every run id the last day's admission verdict log and dispatch records name, and finds for each one a live pointer, a ledger row or a discard or failure record. A run named in those logs with none of the three is a vanished run, and the census finds none. Negative control: the never-launched case against the base revision reaches promotion-requested , and the failing run is logged.",
